Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 17:06:52 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 14/14] MPS-39954 move library modules from
 libraries-misc-plugin to /lib

Drop libraries-misc-plugin.
Cherry-picked c5dab09507410 ignoring changes unrelated to MPS.

DO NOT MERGE TO MASTER!

=== cherry-pick ===

IJPL-248701 Move three misc library modules back to the IDE platform

commons-text, javax.activation and lucene-common were content modules of the
bundled intellij.libraries.misc.plugin wrapper, so they shipped under
lib/modules/. Products that consume them as ordinary platform libraries -- MPS
in particular -- need them as plain jars in lib/.

Introduce CommunityModuleSets.librariesIdeCommon() and nest it in ideCommon(),
mirroring the upstream fix c5dab0950741 for this ticket. This is a partial
backport: only these three modules move, so opencsv, jettison and xstream stay
in the wrapper plugin and it remains bundled everywhere. oshi.core, which
upstream also moved, does not exist on this branch.

The modules are registered with module() rather than embeddedModule(), matching
upstream. The jars therefore land in lib/ but keep their own product-module
classloaders and are not added to product-info.json classPath -- moving them
into the platform classloader would be a separate, riskier change.

Gateway and ReSharper-external bundle the wrapper plugin but never reach
ideCommon(), so they receive the new module set explicitly; without it they
would silently lose javax.activation and lucene-common. The
JetBrainsGatewayBuildTest assertions claiming those two libraries come from the
wrapper are now obsolete and were dropped.

commons-text was the wrapper's only loading="required" anchor. The remaining
three content modules are all optional, which the product-DSL validators accept.

